15. Testing and definition of done
Testing. Write automated tests where this environment can run them. Otherwise write a manual test script in docs/TESTING.md and label the result Implemented, not tested. Prioritize the tests that protect patients and booking logic:
• Authorization: for every protected page and API (CMS, bookings, reports), test the patient, staff and signed-out cases. Test that a second patient account gets "not found" for another account's profiles, bookings and reports. Test that permission keys are enforced (by default Reception cannot release reports or manage the catalogue).
• Bookings: each allowed transition and a sample of forbidden ones; concurrent confirmation of overlapping appointments; accepting and declining a reschedule proposal; the patient cancellation cutoff; the open-request cap; snapshots after a catalogue edit.
• Reports: upload validation (type, size, signature), release, supersede, revoke, download authorization, absence of any public URL, and audit entries.
• Authentication: registration, verification, password reset, no account enumeration, rate-limit responses, session expiry, and a disabled staff account losing its session.
• Localization: every public and patient page renders in both languages; the switch keeps the current page; the fallback note appears for a missing translation; the lang attribute is correct.
• Public site: navbar order and the Explore dropdown by mouse, keyboard and touch; layouts at phone, tablet and desktop widths; sitemap contents; noindex headers on private pages; the CMS route absent from the sitemap, robots.txt, navbar, footer and dashboard.
• CMS: publish and deactivate flows, translation-status display, and staff account creation and disabling.
• Recovery: perform the documented restore once if the environment allows it.
